const UW=RT.unvalidated_why; const fx=(f)=>UW['f_'+f]; const lift=(f,ds)=>fx(f)[ds].lift.toFixed(1); const af=(f,ds)=>fx(f)[ds].attack_fires;
C.push(p([t(`Of the ${RT.n_unified} columns, ${RT.n_unified-RT.n_unvalidated} carry statistical support in at least one dataset under the Table 9 criterion — class association, not causation: the fan-out family’s LMD evidence is the two-regime effect of §3.3 and the credential family’s the composition effect of §4.2 (complete evidence in Figs. 10–11). The remaining ${RT.n_unvalidated} († in Table 9) fail it in both datasets for reasons that differ by feature: the ${RT.unvalidated_by_family.auth_service.length} Security-auditing flags are constant in LMD (no Security channel) and cannot be positive under Mordor’s provenance labels (§3.1.1); the ${RT.unvalidated_by_family.modality.length} modality indicators are context by design; lolbin_parent_child and cmdline_susp fire ${lift('lolbin_parent_child','LMD')}× and ${lift('cmdline_susp','LMD')}× as often in LMD attack rows as in benign rows but on only ${af('lolbin_parent_child','LMD')} and ${af('cmdline_susp','LMD')} attack rows (sparse); rare_dst_pair (lift ${lift('rare_dst_pair','LMD')}) and cmdline_entropy (Cliff’s δ = ${fx('cmdline_entropy').LMD.effect.toFixed(2)}, computed over all rows, most of which carry no command line) are Holm-significant in LMD but below the effect threshold; file_drop_staging is rarer in LMD attack rows than in benign rows and fires ${lift('file_drop_staging','Mordor')}× as often in Mordor attack rows (below the ×3 bar); lsass_access fires on ${af('lsass_access','LMD')} LMD attack rows and ${fx('lsass_access').LMD.benign_fires} benign rows — unscorable by lift and composition rather than specificity, since benign LMD holds a single EID 10 row (§4.2) — and is commoner in benign than in attack rows of Mordor. They remain domain-grounded candidates, not validated inputs, to be tested in Milestone 3 on independently annotated sessions.`)]));
