const W14=[1350,1400,3300,3310];
const T14=[
 ['Random Forest','Supervised, bagging','ŷ = mode{hᵢ(x)}, i = 1…B; the B trees are grown on bootstrap samples with √d features per split.','Non-linear interactions across mixed families, robust to residual redundancy, no scaling; continuity with the Chapter-4 ranking.'],
 ['LightGBM','Supervised, boosting','Fₙ(x) = Fₙ₋₁(x) + η·hₙ(x); leaf-wise growth on histogram splits.','Primary classifier: learns conjunctions such as inbound-admin-port ∧ remote-exec lineage ∧ velocity; class weights handle 8%/4% prevalence at 10⁶ rows.'],
 ['LSTM','Deep, sequential','cₜ = fₜ⊙cₜ₋₁ + iₜ⊙c̃ₜ with input/forget/output gates over an ordered sequence.','Lateral movement is a multi-stage sequence (logon → remote-exec → tool drop → credential access); recurrence models the order — only with sequence framing (below).'],
 ['Isolation Forest','Unsupervised, anomaly','s(x, n) = 2^(−E[h(x)]/c(n)); anomalies isolate in short random paths.','Label-free first-line filter for unseen tradecraft; natural where labels are weak (Mordor).'],
];
const t14=[headerRow(['Model','Paradigm','Mathematical basis','Fit to threat and features'],W14)];
T14.forEach((r,i)=>t14.push(drow(r,W14,i,{size:15,boldCol0:true})));
C.push(table(W14,t14)); C.push(tcap(11,'Four selected models across the three required paradigms.'));
C.push(p([t('LSTM sequence framing. ',{bold:true}),t(`An LSTM needs a tensor of shape (batch, T, D). Events are ordered by timestamp per host; a window is the T = 20 events of the host ending at a given event (windows end at every 4th event in LMD and every 2nd in Mordor, for cost), and a shorter history is pre-padded with unmasked zero vectors. Each timestep is the ${RT.n_unified}-column schema with event_category one-hot over the registry’s ${RT.n_registry_levels} levels (${RT.n_event_categories} of them observed here; ${RT.n_unified} − 1 + ${RT.n_registry_levels} = ${RT.D_lstm_registry} inputs), scaled per §5.3; the window carries the label of its last event, giving a causal per-event decision comparable with the row-level models. Stacked LSTM (64 → 32 units), dropout 0.3, batch normalisation, class-weighted cross-entropy, Adam at 10⁻³, early stopping on a grouped inner hold-out (tuned in Milestone 3). The LSTM baselines in [2, 3] consume per-event vectors (T = 1), so their scores are not sequence-model benchmarks for this framing.`)]));
C.push(h2('6.2 State-of-the-Art Literature Synthesis'));
