C.push(p([t('Synthesis (Table 12). ',{bold:true}),t('Tree ensembles are the strongest, cheapest tabular baselines for Sysmon LM data [2, 3]; unsupervised detectors reach ≈95% AUC on LMD-2023 [4], and Isolation Forest is a common label-free baseline on user/host telemetry [11] (Table 12 notes its evaluation caveat); behavioural window features drive the LANL results [1, 5]. The supervised LMD-2023 benchmarks rest on capture identifiers — seven calendar fields in [2] (F1 99.41%), CompSTA and EventRecordID in [3] — and §3.3 and Table 8 show why such scores are a property of the capture; Milestone 3 therefore reports cross-dataset and within-Mordor grouped-split results beside the LMD figures and treats the gap as the finding.')]));

